From: Codex <codex@local>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: cvitek: do not claim mailboxes for an empty table

The mailbox-only C906L firmware can include a valid 16-byte resource-table
header with num == 0.  table_ptr is non-NULL for that firmware, but there are
no virtqueues to notify.  Claiming the channels pins the mailbox driver and
makes the vendor cmdqu probe fail with EBUSY when the media stack starts.

Treat an empty table like an absent table, retaining the existing behavior
for firmware with resource entries.

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/cvitek_remoteproc.c b/drivers/remoteproc/cvitek_remoteproc.c
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/cvitek_remoteproc.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/cvitek_remoteproc.c
@@ -594,7 +594,9 @@ static int cvitek_rproc_start(struct rproc *rproc)
 	dev_dbg(&rproc->dev, "Starting\n");
 
 
-	if (ddata->mbox_client_vq.dev && rproc->table_ptr) {
+	/* An empty resource table has no virtqueues and needs no mailbox. */
+	if (ddata->mbox_client_vq.dev && rproc->table_ptr &&
+	    rproc->table_ptr->num) {
 		/*
 		* To control a co-processor without IPC mechanism.
 		* This driver can be used without mbox and rpmsg.
